    "rationale": "Two active, unconditioned records at repository scope with 'reviewed' trust answer the question directly: a repeated request key returns the first successful response kept in its idempotency receipt. 5c53ca49 (request identity) is backed by the HTTP acceptance probe (fixture://quality/receipt-a). 429ebfbe (financial reconciliation) is backed by the independent queue probe (fixture://quality/receipt-b). They agree and are kept as separate evidence, not merged. Bounded retries (9a2b24a7) is supporting context: it keeps the request identifier the same across attempts. Excluded: the repeated pagination cursor record (different subject), plus two candidates filtered out for a missing prerequisite or not applying. The transactions branches (component:src/transactions) were left unexpanded because the component context is unknown, so some uncertainty remains about component-specific replay rules. These are untrusted synthetic records whose claims have not been checked against code."
